    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_002",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_meaning_units"
      ],
      "title": "Where the Object Goes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Some particle verbs take an object, which is the person or thing affected by the action. With a noun object, Norwegian often allows the noun before or after the particle. With a pronoun object, such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "den",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "det",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ham",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", the pronoun normally comes before the particle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Noun object: verb plus noun plus particle is common; verb plus particle plus noun is also possible with many everyday particle verbs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kan du skru ovnen av?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Can you turn the oven off?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kan du skru av ovnen?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Can you turn off the oven?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Pronoun object: put the pronoun before the particle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kan du skru den av?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Can you turn it off?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg tar den med."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I am bringing it along."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Avoid placing a pronoun after the particle in these object patterns. "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Skru av den",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " is not the natural choice when "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "den",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " means the object being turned off."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_003",
      "role": "recap",
      "objective_ids": [],
      "title": "Use the Verb and Particle Together",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When you meet a particle verb, first read the verb and particle together as one meaning unit. Then check whether there is an object, and whether that object is a noun or a pronoun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Learn the whole meaning: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "slå på",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " means turn on."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "With a noun object, both positions may be possible: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "slå på lyset",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "slå lyset på",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "With a pronoun object, place the pronoun before the particle: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "slå det på",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
